# Docker build context excludes.
#
# railway.toml sets context = ".", so the whole repo is the build context even
# though the Dockerfile only needs ivr-router/. Anything listed here is never
# uploaded to the daemon and can never end up in an image layer.

# --- Secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
# .env is gitignored, so it never reaches Railway (which builds from git), but a
# local `docker build` would otherwise bake real credentials into a layer where
# they survive even if a later step deletes them. The app reads its config from
# environment variables in production; dotenv no-ops when no .env is present.
**/.env
**/.env.*

# --- Dependencies ------------------------------------------------------------
# The image runs `npm install --omit=dev`. Copying a host-built tree in would
# shadow that install, drag dev dependencies into production, and ship native
# modules compiled for the host rather than node:22-alpine. This is also 57MB
# of the 69MB context.
**/node_modules

# --- VCS and agent tooling ---------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.claude

# --- Logs, caches, build output ----------------------------------------------
**/*.log
**/npm-debug.log*
**/.DS_Store
**/dist
**/build
**/coverage
**/.nyc_output
**/.vscode
**/.idea

# --- Docs and design assets --------------------------------------------------
# Not read at runtime. Note ivr-router/public/console.html IS served by the
# /console route, so HTML is excluded only at the repo root, never recursively.
*.md
**/*.md
/*.html
/*.dc.html
/canvas.json
